scope: |
  Orphan drain batch 4. install-sh-reports-failure-gate.sh has been an orphan since it was
  written, and the toolchain cache (2026-08-09) moved in front of the path it tests three days
  later: on a digest HIT install.sh restores bin/lib and never calls sbt, so row 1 passed for an
  unrelated reason (publishLocal) and row 2 read the cache's exit 0 as "the defect is back".
  The witness in install.sh is intact — proven by deleting it and watching row 2 go red.
  Fix: cache off for both rows, reachability asserted before any verdict, each row asserts the
  MECHANISM string, and the gate asserts it left the toolchain it borrowed unchanged (the HIT
  path did `rm -rf bin/lib` in the shared checkout, twice per run). Then unfreeze it in
  no-orphan-gates.sh and wire it into conformance-extras (2 s). ci.yml touched at the END of that
  job's batch block only.
